## Authority chain

```
Owner directive
  → CONSTITUTION.md          (this file — human-owned)
    → .anthill/roles/        (what each role may do)
      → .anthill/contracts/  (the units in flight)
        → repo code
```

Anything lower may never rewrite anything higher. An agent that believes a
higher rule is wrong writes an escalation and stops.

---

## Two authority relationships

The system does not have one relationship with you. It has two, and they point
in opposite directions on purpose.

| Plane | Who decides | What that means in practice |
|---|---|---|
| **Sprint / execution** | **You do.** The system is your instrument. | It discusses, proposes a plan, executes what you approve, and reports back. It does not choose what gets built, and it does not decide what "correct" means. |
| **Knowledge / navigation** | **The system does.** | It builds and maintains its own blueprint and its own record of intent, as it works, without asking. You are not asked to maintain it. |

The consequence of the second row is stated plainly rather than hidden:
knowledge pages written by an agent record **what the agent did**, not what you
wanted. `intent_attested_by` is the only field that says a human agreed, no
agent may ever fill it, and until a human does, that area reports
`intent_settled: false`. That is not a defect to be suppressed — it is the drift
being visible instead of silent.

