## Rules

- No new dependencies without owner approval.
- No scope changes without a sprint entry.
- Contracts are the source of truth for any interface between units. Interfaces
  are never defined inline in a unit brief.
- No agent modifies another agent's scope. Ownership is enforced, not requested.
- An agent never asserts its own completion. Only a passing gate closes a unit.
- An audit may refuse a unit. An audit may never, by itself, pass one.
- Protected paths (below) are never edited by any agent, for any reason.

## Protected paths

These bind the agents, so the agents may not reach them. Editing any of these is
an owner action performed outside a unit.

```text
/CONSTITUTION.md
/.anthill/roles/
/.anthill/anthill.config.json
/.anthill/contracts/
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/.claude/
```

